in an isothermal oven for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ . After centrifugation at $10000\mathrm{rpm}$ for $2\mathrm{min}$ , the clear supernatant was carefully collected in a $20\mathrm{mL}$ Pyrex vial. UiO- $67(\mathrm{Zr})$ seed crystals in $1\mathrm{mL}$ DMF were added to the vial. The mixture was gently stirred with a magnetic stir bar $\left(60\mathrm{rpm}\right)$ at $25~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for 19 hours. The reaction suspension was centrifuged at $10000\mathrm{rpm}$ for $2\mathrm{min}$ to obtain UiO- $67(\mathrm{Zr}){\bf{\in}}\mathrm{UiO}{-67(\mathrm{Hf})}$ product in the form of white precipitate. The product was then washed with fresh DMF $\left(4\mathrm{mL},4\mathrm{x}\right)$ .
Postsynthetic metalation of Bpy-UiO-67 ${\bf\langle{Z r}\rangle{\bf{{\in U i O-}}}67(Z r)}$ . Bis(acetonitrile)dichloropalladium(II) $(10.4~\mathrm{mg},0.04~\mathrm{mmol})$ ) was dissolved in $3~\mathrm{\mL}$ acetonitrile in a $4~\mathrm{mL}$ Pyrex vial. The Bis(acetonitrile)dichloropalladium(II) solution was then mixed with $1\ \mathrm{mL}$ acetonitrile suspension of $\mathrm{Bpy-UiO-}67(\mathrm{Zr}){\bf\in}\mathrm{UiO}.$ $67(\mathrm{Zr})$ (containing ${\sim}0.033$ mmol BpyDC). The mixture was placed at room temperature for $24\mathrm{h}$ .  After centrifugation at 10,000 rpm for $2\ \mathrm{min}$ , yellow precipitate was collected and copiously wash with acetonitrile $(6\mathrm{mL},6\mathrm{x})$ .
Postsynthetic metalation of $\mathbf{Bpy-UiO-67(Zr){\bf{\in}}}\mathbf{Pro-UiO-67(Zr)}$ . Bpy-UiO- ${\cdot67(\mathrm{Zr})}{\subset}\mathrm{Pro.UiO}{\cdot67(\mathrm{Zr})}$ ( $\mathrm{34.4~mg,}$ containing $\sim0.03$ mmol bipyridine linker) was suspended in $1\ \mathrm{mL}$ acetonitrile. Bis(acetonitrile)dichloropalladium(II) (7.5 mg, 0.031 mmol) dissolved in acetonitrile $(6\mathrm{mL})$ was added to the MOF suspension. The mixture was allowed to react at room temperature for $24\mathrm{h}$ and then centrifuged at $10,000\mathrm{rpm}$ for $2\mathrm{min}$ . The yellow precipitate was collected and profusely washed with acetonitrile $(6\mathrm{mL},6\mathrm{x})$ .
Syntheses of $\mathrm{^{\prime}C u_{2-}S e=U i O-67(Z r)=U i O-67(H f)}0.4M$ solution of $\mathrm{Zr(O^{\eta}P r)_{4}}$ in $\mathrm{CH_{3}C O O H}$ was prepared by mixing $\mathrm{Zr}\mathrm{(O^{\prime}P r)}_{4}70$ wt. $\%$ in $n$ -propanol $\left(187.2\mathrm{mg},0.04\mathrm{mmol}\right)$ with $\mathrm{CH_{3}C O O H}$ (1 mL). $\mathbf{A}0.02\mathbf{M}$ solution of $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ -BPDC in DMF was prepared by heating a mixture of $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ -BPDC $(19.4\mathrm{mg},0.08\mathrm{mmol})$ ) and DMF $\left(4\mathrm{mL}\right)$ ) on a stir plate at $150^{\mathrm{oC}}$ until complete dissolution. To a $20\mathrm{mL}$ Pyrex vial were added in sequence $\mathrm{CH_{3}C O O H}$ ( $\mathrm{.}1.2~\mathrm{mL}$ ), 0.4 M $\mathrm{Zr(O^{\eta}P r)_{4}}$ solution $\left(0.2\mathrm{mL},0.08\mathrm{mmol}\right)$ , DMF $\ensuremath{\left(4\mathrm{mL}\right)}$ and $0.02\mathrm{MH}_{2}$ -BPDC solution $\left(4\mathrm{mL},0.08\mathrm{mmol}\right)$ , $\mathrm{Cu}_{2\cdot\mathrm{x}}\mathrm{Se}$ nanoparticle EtOH solution (8 $\mathrm{mL},$ , Optical Density ${\sim}0.2$ at $1085\mathrm{nm}$ ).  The mixture was allowed to react at $25^{\mathsf{\circ}}\mathsf{C}$ for $40\mathrm{min}$ to yield turbid suspension. The suspension was centrifuged at $10000~\mathrm{rpm}$ for $2~\mathrm{min}$ to obtain dark green $\mathrm{Cu}_{2}$ - ${}_{\mathrm{{x}}}S{\mathrm{{e}}}{=}\mathrm{{UiO}}{-}67(\mathrm{{Zr}})$ precipitate. The precipitate was washed with fresh DMF $\left(4\mathrm{mL},4\mathrm{x}\right)$ . $\mathrm{Cu_{2-x}S e{=}U i O{-}}67\mathrm{(Zr)}$ was then used as seeds to undergo epitaxial growth to afford $\mathrm{Cu}_{2\cdot\mathrm{x}}\mathrm{Se}{\bf\in}\mathrm{UiO}{\cdot}67(\mathrm{Zr}){\bf\in}\mathrm{UiO}{\cdot}$ 67(Hf). Detailed conditions can be found in supporting information. Detailed syntheses o $\mathrm{\cdotAu{\bf{\bar{c}}}U i O-67(Z r){\bf{\bar{c}}}U i O-67(H f)}$ and $\mathrm{Ag}{\bf\mathsf{=U i O-}}67(\mathrm{Zr}){\bf\mathsf{=U i O-}}67(\mathrm{Hf})$ can also be found in supporting 